<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Supreme Council of the Irish Confederation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1642–1649</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Supreme Council was the executive of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederate-ireland">Confederate Ireland</a>, the Catholic government set up at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a> in 1642 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-confederate-wars">Irish Confederate Wars</a>. Chosen by the General Assembly, it raised armies, levied taxes and negotiated with Charles I and the papal nuncio Rinuccini. The confederation dissolved in 1649, shortly before Cromwell's invasion.</p></div>
